{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLDWvy2aDXFN4z753BpV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I marked issue #221 as **blocked** and wrote `.ard/221/triage-lead.md`.\n\nThe request itself is a clear change: post one comment on the status issue when a scanner starts failing, and one when it recovers. It's blocked because one of the failure types it must report is the pre-filing secret guard from #215, and that guard isn't in the code yet. `docs/TODO.md` still lists #215 as open, and `internal/scanner/pipeline.go` has no guard. The other two failure types, a `scan_failed` run and a scanner skipped at `max_open`, are already in the code.\n\n**Routing once #215 lands:**\n- **`triage:engineer`:** the only triage role besides lead in this repository, so it's the only one to ask.\n- **Worker:** engineer.\n- **Reviewers:** `eng-review` needs no entry, because `.ard/config.yaml` gives it no `when:` rule, so it runs on every pull request anyway.\n\n**Things I noted for a maintainer in the file:**\n- The issue says it must land before #217, so #217 now waits on this one as well.\n- The change adds data to scanner state. There's no architect role here, so the engineer's plan needs to cover that schema change and its migration.\n- A maintainer could instead start now with `scan_failed` and `max_open`, and add the guard type when #215 lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":900,"cache_read_input_tokens":12646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":900},"output_tokens":441,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"547e150e-7c8d-4b48-a151-79fbd3726836","uuid":"96676494-0cef-4c78-a42b-3eda0b30ecab","timestamp":"2026-11-23T16:59:49.684Z","